Ulrich Eckhardt wrote:
>
> I wonder why events that inflame (is that the right word for that, btw?)
> things like scrolls or make potions boil don't also activate oil lamps?

In the code there are plenty of events that can go wrong on the
spot, but few events that can go wrong a long time later.  I think
this is a deliberate design intent by the DevTeam.  Turning to
stone starts a short clock to death with knowable fixes.  Eating
a spoiled corpse gives food poisoning and starts a medium clock
to death with knowable fixes.

I think lamps don't turn on for the same reason wands might
explode but they don't lose some number of zaps - It makes
game play worse and is also a lot of work to code.  Even though
turning a lamp on is easy to code other similar events aren't.



